# T-2793 — Addressed-post canary (the symmetric-inbox miss, G-063 sibling)
# Source of truth: /opt/termlink/.context/cron/addressed-posts-canary.crontab (git-tracked)
# Installed to:    /etc/cron.d/termlink-addressed-posts-canary (USER field syntax — do NOT load into a user crontab)
#
# On 2026-08-18 two independent operators — this agent and 999-AEF — each wrote a post
# to agent-chat-arc naming the other as recipient, and each found the other's only by
# sweeping the topic by hand. Both posts were durable and both arrived: delivery was
# never the problem, ADDRESSING was. To every surfacing verb either side owned, a post
# that names its recipient is an undifferentiated broadcast, and the unread count is
# honest but useless — it says "something happened" on a topic where a -vendored
# heartbeat lands hourly. 999-AEF at arc @114: "Symmetric failure, both directions,
# which is a stronger signal than either of us hitting it alone."
#
# The capability was already there and dark. T-1513 shipped metadata.mentions plus
# `agent mentions` / `channel mentions-of` to read it; at filing, `agent mentions '*'`
# returned [] across all 115 envelopes and no script set the field or read it in any
# daily path. That is the T-2683 class (a capability nothing executes) in the comms rail.
#
# FIRES (exit 1) when a post addresses you — by metadata.mentions OR by an alias in
# .context/checks/addressed-aliases — and sits past your ack frontier on the topic.
# Empty log = healthy. /canaries auto-discovers this log.
#
# --self-id is pinned because identity does not resolve on this host: `whoami` is
# ambiguous here (the T-2690 PID-ancestor case) and no be-reachable.state carries an
# agent_id. Without it the check still runs but loses the ack frontier and reports every
# addressed post on every run — safe, but it would fill the log daily and destroy the
# "empty = healthy" one-bit channel. Re-derive it from `channel ack-status <topic> --json`
# if this host's fingerprint ever changes.
#
# Operator action on firing: read the named offsets, reply (/reply or /agent-handoff),
# then ack the topic — `termlink channel ack agent-chat-arc --up-to <offset>` — which is
# what silences it. Ad-hoc: bash scripts/check-addressed-posts.sh
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Every 4 hours at :47 — deliberately NOT daily. This one is latency-sensitive in a way
# the fitness canaries are not: the cost being prevented is a peer waiting on a reply,
# and the miss it was built from ran ~2h before a hand sweep caught it. A 24h cadence
# would have detected that miss no sooner than the human did.
47 */4 * * * root cd /opt/termlink && bash scripts/check-addressed-posts.sh --quiet --self-id d1993c2c3ec44c94 >> .context/working/.addressed-posts-canary.log 2>> .context/working/.addressed-posts-canary.log.stderr
